  "details": "Currently the steam frame controllers have a few very minor issues.\n\nThe thumb position is backwards due to the thumbstick location. For example, if your right hand's thumb is on the thumbstick, and you move it to the right to touch the buttons, your avatar's thumb actually moves left. This is very minor, and doesn't really matter.\n\nWhen naturally making a 'fist' with a steam frame controller, your pointer and middle finger will not close unless you squeeze the grip and trigger buttons. On the index, this was not the case, simply resting your fingers in the position was good enough. This makes doing gestures a little weird.\n\nI believe this last point is more of a steam issue than VRChat, but the bindings call the controllers either an xbox controller, or oculus touch controller, which means the default bindings are really wacky, and changing them is currently complicated on Steam Frame. It's doable... but we do need some official bindings for sure!",
